            </summary>
            <div class="p-4 text-stone-700 leading-relaxed">
              The Poconos around Scranton and Wilkes-Barre top out around 2,100 feet at Big Pocono/Camelback
              Mountain — real terrain, but not the kind of named-summit trail this guide tracks. The nearest
              tracked mountains are on New Jersey's Kittatinny Ridge, starting under an hour east, with the
              Catskills and the Hudson Highlands reachable as a farther day trip.
            </div>
          </details>

          <details class="group">
